From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: FontIcon

FontIcon, the icon element most apps use for their icon-font glyphs, did not exist: markup with it failed and AppBarButtons with a FontIcon had no icon. It now exists -- activated, composed or from markup, with Glyph, FontSize (20), FontFamily (the icon font), FontWeight and FontStyle and their dependency properties -- and draws its glyph in its Foreground like SymbolIcon; when the icon font is missing its glyphs are drawn as the standard characters of 6158. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
